# Environment variables Pages still reads.
#
# Port, database path, and the setup state are not configured here: they live
# in ~/.pages/config.toml (see README), and start parameters such as --port
# override that file. The variables below are optional runtime switches.
#
# Pages does not load this file by itself. Export the variables in the shell
# or in the service definition, or start the server with
# `node --env-file=.env server.mjs`.

# Instance key for stored GitHub tokens and agent API keys: 64 hexadecimal characters
# (32 bytes). Without it, Pages creates a key file next to the database.
# Agent API keys use a separate HKDF-derived encryption key. Existing GitHub
# tokens keep their original format. Back up this key with the database;
# neither kind of secret can be decrypted without it. CLI credentials live
# separately in the agents folder beside the database and need a protected backup.
# PAGES_GITHUB_TOKEN_KEY=

# Secure attribute of the session and language cookies: true or false.
# Default: set when the request came in over HTTPS (also as reported by a
# reverse proxy in X-Forwarded-Proto), not set over plain HTTP. Browsers drop
# Secure cookies on plain HTTP outside of localhost.
# PAGES_COOKIE_SECURE=

# Set to 1 to log server cache hits, misses and invalidations.
# PAGES_CACHE_DEBUG=

# Development only: log statements slower than this many milliseconds
# (default 50).
# PAGES_SLOW_QUERY_MS=

# Optional narrowing of the local directories agent workspaces may use,
# separated by the OS path delimiter (colon on Linux). Unset or empty: no
# variable is needed, and every existing directory of this machine that the
# account running Pages can read, write and traverse qualifies. The folder
# browser of the workspace dialog then opens at that account's home directory;
# with the variable set it lists directories only within these roots.
# Roots and directories are canonicalized; Pages instance data and overlapping
# registrations are always excluded. This allowlist is not an execution sandbox.
# PAGES_WORKSPACE_ROOTS=

# Built Pages MCP bundle that CLI sessions of ticket-bound plan nodes start
# (stdio). Default: mcp/dist/pages-mcp-v<version>.cjs below the start directory.
# A ticket-bound node fails before its start when the bundle is not readable.
# PAGES_MCP_BUNDLE=

# Web and API address of this instance for those local MCP processes, without
# a trailing slash. Default: http://127.0.0.1:<configured port>.
# PAGES_AGENT_API_URL=

# Mode of the production server; server.mjs sets production when unset.
# NODE_ENV=production

# Discord notifications of projects (Projects -> Interfaces -> Discord). One
# Discord application serves the whole instance; all three values are secrets of
# the server and are never sent to a browser or written to a log. Without them
# the Discord panel only explains what is missing. See "Discord notifications"
# in the README for the setup in the Discord Developer Portal.
# Application ID (the OAuth2 client ID):
# PAGES_DISCORD_APPLICATION_ID=
# OAuth2 client secret:
# PAGES_DISCORD_CLIENT_SECRET=
# Bot token:
# PAGES_DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN=

# Public address of this instance, without a trailing slash, for the Discord
# redirect `<address>/discord/callback` and the links in Discord messages. Set it
# behind a reverse proxy or when the phone that scans the QR code reaches Pages
# under another address than the server sees. Default: the address of the request
# that starts the connection.
# PAGES_PUBLIC_URL=

# Native ACP resource admission (PAGE-81); both Codex and Claude share this limit.
# PAGES_MAX_CONCURRENT_ACP_SESSIONS=1
# PAGES_ACP_MEMORY_AWARE=true
# PAGES_ACP_MIN_AVAILABLE_MEMORY_MB=2048
